  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following is not correct?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Rusting of iron can be stopped by increasing the concentration of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>  in water",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Rusting of iron is electrochemical in nature",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Rusting of iron takes place in moist air",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Rusting of iron produces hydrated iron (III) oxide",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Rusting of iron is an electrochemical phenomenon in which one spot of iron acts as anode.<br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> <br/><br/>These electrons move through the metal and are taken up by the oxygen already dissolved in water in presence of  <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  furnished by  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> , which is formed by the dissolution of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>  in water. The concentration of  <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  depends upon the concentration of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>  in water.<br/><br/>Cathode  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">q</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <br/><br/>Since increase in the concentration of  <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  results in the increase in the rate of the reaction, therefore, rusting of iron occurs quicker, when the concentration of dissolved  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>  in water increases.<br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  so-obtained are further oxidized to  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  by atmospheric oxygen.  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  is then hydrated to form rust.<br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>→</mo><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></munder></math>"
